            {
              "id": "54e9c1f0-08c2-34af-8148-2da1a8a3223e",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Vulnerable Hash Algorithm\" vulnerability refers to the use of weak or broken cryptographic hash functions in a software application. In this case, the MD5 hash function is used, which is considered insecure for many cryptographic purposes because it is susceptible to hash collisions. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to produce the same hash output using different input, leading to potential security risks such as unauthorized access or data integrity issues.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use a stronger, more secure hash function such as SHA-256 or SHA-3. These hash functions are currently considered secure and are not susceptible to known vulnerabilities like MD5.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the use of MD5 with a more secure hash function. Here is an example of how you might do this using SHA-256:\n\n```cpp\n#include <openssl/sha.h>\n\nstd::string sha256(const std::string str)\n{\n    unsigned char hash[SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH];\n    SHA256_CTX sha256;\n    SHA256_Init(&sha256);\n    SHA256_Update(&sha256, str.c_str(), str.size());\n    SHA256_Final(hash, &sha256);\n    std::stringstream ss;\n    for(int i = 0; i < SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH; i++)\n    {\n        ss << std::hex << std::setw(2) << std::setfill('0') << (int)hash[i];\n    }\n    return ss.str();\n}\n\n// Usage\nif (sha256(hsaco) == static_cast<std::string>(sha256_sum)) {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the OpenSSL library to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS126858",
                  "54e9c1f0-08c2-34af-8148-2da1a8a3223e"
                ]
              }
